Skipping & Disabling Checks (Code Manager Governance)                         

1. Global Skip (via Commit/PR Message)                                        

You can disable an entire CI job globally by including                        
`ci-ignore: <job_name>` in your commit message or PR description during       
emergency hotfixes.                                                           

Example: `git commit -m "Updating docs. ci-ignore: yamllint"`                 

Available tags: `yamllint`, `yamllint_scientific`, `implementation_standard`, 
`bash_shellcheck`, `shebang_script`, `bash_setx`, `bash_exitzero`,            
`python_flake8`, `python_pytest`.                                             

2. File-level Skip (via Inline Comment)                                       

Place a comment in the specific file to bypass checks for that file only.     

Example in YAML: `# ci-ignore: yamllint_scientific`                           
Example in Bash: `# ci-ignore: bash_setx`                                     

3. Repository-level Skip (via `.lst` Files)                                   

Code Managers can permanently exclude files or directories by adding their    
relative paths to the corresponding `.lst` file in `.github/workflows/`.      
